  "id": "COMPOUND:27856 - PROTEIN:1026",
  "verbalization": "Tasumatrol I(rel) is shown to interact with multiple targets that ultimately lead to the inhibition of Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor 1. The first pathway links Tasumatrol I(rel) to Potassium channel subfamily K member 9, which is then targeted by a compound that itself targets Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor 1. This suggests a direct interaction between Tasumatrol I(rel) and a downstream target that ultimately affects the activity of Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitors. The second pathway reveals that Tasumatrol I(rel) also targets another protein, Potassium channel subfamily K member 9, which is further targeted by 3-anhydro-6-hydroxy-ophiobolin A, which in turn targets Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor 1. The third pathway shows that Tasumatrol I(rel) interacts with DNA gyrase subunit B, which is targeted by a complex compound that also targets Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor 1. These findings collectively suggest that Tasumatrol I(rel) may exert its effects through multiple distinct mechanisms that ultimately result in the inhibition of Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitors. The evidence supports a complex network of interactions, where Tasumatrol I(rel) may act through different pathways to modulate the activity of Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitors, potentially through the inhibition of potassium channels or DNA gyrase. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Tasumatrol I(rel) to have a broad impact on cellular processes involving cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitors.",
